# What a test run reads to reach a real service instead of a fake. Copy this file to
# `.env.local.tests`, which git ignores, and fill in only the services you want that run to meet.
# A value left empty keeps its fake, so one file gives you every combination.
#
#   bun run hetzner
#
# Nothing loads this file on its own. Bun reads `.env` and `.env.test` into every `bun test`, and
# `bun check` fails if either exists here, because a credential in one would mean a plain
# `bun test` spending money at a real provider.
#
# See `docs/setups/hetzner-cloud.md`. A project that holds nothing else: the run makes its own
# firewall, labels everything it creates, removes all of it at the end, and removes what a killed
# run left behind, so anything still in that project afterwards is a leak.
HCLOUD_TOKEN=
